{"id": "EUVD-2026-103065", "enisaUuid": "9ae0c2b1-7859-35c8-90e4-989bdddfd1a6", "description": "Misaka Danmu Server through 2.8.9 contains an authentication bypass vulnerability that allows unauthenticated attackers to write arbitrary configuration keys via the unprotected POST /api/ui/config-history/rollback endpoint. Attackers can set the ipWhitelist key to their own /32 address, or alter trustedProxies and webhookApiKey, to access every protected endpoint as the administrator.", "datePublished": "2026-10-16T17:39:13", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T17:39:13", "baseScore": 9.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@hieuPenguinnn/misaka-danmu-server-ui-api-missing-authentication", "https://github.com/l429609201/misaka_danmu_server/blob/v2.8.9/src/api/ui/config_history.py#L51-L66", "https://github.com/l429609201/misaka_danmu_server/blob/v2.8.9/src/security.py#L136-L182", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/misaka-danmu-server-through-2.8.9-authentication-bypass-via-config-history-rollback"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111643", "GHSA-h9w3-vw4p-h6vw"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.45, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "edf4fad5-e6ed-35e4-b4b7-4f341cb8563a", "product": {"name": "misaka_danmu_server", "vendor": {"name": "l429609201"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22642.8.9"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "13c3f9fb-f66e-35f5-b47b-81d758ef9688", "vendor": {"name": "l429609201"}}], "isExploited": false}